# Track nothing by default; name the source explicitly below.
#
# This way round because the two sets are shaped differently. The SOURCE is a
# handful of directories that changes about never. The GENERATED half cannot be
# enumerated at all: agents work in directories named by each role's `cwd` in
# Configs/roles/<role>/role.toml, so a new role invents a new output directory
# without touching this file. Denylisting an open-ended set means every new
# role is one forgotten line away from committing an agent's workspace.
#
# The cost, stated plainly: a new source file in a directory NOT listed below
# is invisible to git, and `git add` will say nothing about it. If you add a
# top-level directory, add it here in the same commit.
*

# Descend into directories anyway. Without this nothing below can match: git
# does not look inside an ignored directory, so the negations never get a
# chance. Directories are not objects in git, so this tracks nothing by itself.
!*/

# The source. Everything installable lives under one directory, so adding a
# package is no longer a line here.
!/src/**
# Not under `src/`, and not by oversight: nothing imports it. The plugin is
# installed into the tool, which launches `server.py` by path, so making it a
# package would only offer a second way to reach a file that is already found.
!/plugins/**
# The marketplace manifest that makes `/plugin marketplace add .` work. One
# file rather than `!/.claude-plugin/**`: a directory negation here would also
# track whatever the tool decides to cache next to it.
!/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json
!/gateway/**
!/configs/**
!/tests/**

# The adapters themselves are deployment state, but the envelope format they
# have to produce is not.
!/inputs.d/README.md

# This file, the front door, and how the source above gets installed.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/pyproject.toml

# Re-ignored last: the negations above are broad enough to sweep these back in
# from inside a source directory, and a later rule wins.
# Its own repository, cloned in. See the README.
/state_store/

# Build output, and it lands INSIDE the source directory: `pip install -e .`
# writes it next to the packages, where `!/src/**` sweeps it straight back in.
# The one case the deny-by-default rule above does not already cover, because
# it is generated into the half of the tree that is named explicitly.
/src/*.egg-info/
/build/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
